{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux relies on specific patterns to ensure correct ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" behavior, efficient rendering, and safe concurrency. This article explains the reasoning behind these patterns.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"The Snapshot Pattern","anchor":"The-Snapshot-Pattern","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send()"},{"type":"text","text":" copies the observer tree into a local struct, mutates the copy via the reducer, then assigns changed properties back. This happens internally via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State(observer:)"},{"type":"text","text":" packs, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply(_:to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" unpacks."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The pattern exists for two reasons:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" equality checking."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor checks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and suppresses no-op notifications. Swift’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_modify"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor (used by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout"},{"type":"text","text":") fires notifications unconditionally. The snapshot pattern routes through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cross-slice observation isolation."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates a separate "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" class for each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" property. A view reading "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.items"},{"type":"text","text":" won’t re-render when only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"type":"text","text":" changes, because they live on different observer objects."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates the observer class tree and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance automatically. Hand-written conformance is still possible for advanced cases — see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explicit equality guards ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"if x != state.x { x = state.x }"},{"type":"text","text":") are unnecessary. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" already checks equality on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":". Unconditional assignment is safe."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside"},{"text":"Dispatch Loop Detection","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"text":" warns if ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called more than 100 times per debounce interval. This usually means ","type":"text"},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" isn’t using the snapshot pattern, causing cascading re-renders that trigger re-dispatches.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Reducer Weight","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Reducer-Weight"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and dispatch the result back as an action."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Effect Threading","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Effect-Threading"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"type":"text","text":". Blocking calls ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Process.waitUntilExit()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes."}]}],"style":"important","name":"Important","type":"aside"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use async alternatives: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"terminationHandler"},{"text":" + continuation instead of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"waitUntilExit()"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task.sleep()"},{"text":" instead of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.sleep()"},{"text":", async file I\/O instead of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data(contentsOf:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"],"title":"Explanation","generated":true,"anchor":"Explanation"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxObservable":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Bridges a value-type state struct to an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" class tree for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-property SwiftUI observation granularity."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","title":"SwiduxObservable","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxObservable","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxobservable","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxObservable","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"Effect","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","title":"Plugin Architecture","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"Swidux","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","title":"Design Principles","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}]}}}